{
 "updated": "2026-10-15",
 "notes": [
  "Home Affairs no longer publishes occupation ceilings on immi.homeaffairs.gov.au (the page was removed in 2021). The only official per-occupation ceiling table found is the 2025-26 table released under FOI FA 26/01/00545; no official 2024-25 or 2026-27 table was found as of 2026-10-15.",
  "Ceilings apply to subclass 189 and subclass 491 (Family Sponsored) only, not to 190 or state-nominated 491 or employer-sponsored visas. They are policy guidance, subject to change.",
  "ceiling = \"Occupation Ceiling adjusted\" (average 2024-25 ABS employment stock x tier multiplier, minimum 500). grantsPY2425 = 2024-25 grants under 491/494/186/190. remaining189 = places left for subclass 189 in 2025-26.",
  "Raw fields keep the published text: \"-\" means no places remain (grants already exceed the ceiling), \"<5\" and \"<500\" are masked values; the numeric field is null in those cases.",
  "Unit groups not in the table had no ceiling listed in the release. Only 87 unit groups are covered.",
  "Average stock for 2411 is 79172 in the table but 79,171 in FOI FA 25/10/01376; the table value is used."
 ],
